  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Senya is looking very sick after drinking some bad alcohol. Fedya talks to him about his stomach. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты выглядишь совсем плохо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "У тебя болит живот?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Да, мне очень плохо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я же тебе говорил.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не надо было есть рыбу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я думал, она нормальная.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Знаешь, что надо делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Надо выпить перец и воду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ой, я больше не могу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сеня, что с тобой?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сеня, открой глаза! Сеня!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Понятно, давай дальше.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты выглядишь совсем плохо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You look completely bad.' Fedya uses the casual singular 'you' with 'you', as close colleagues and friends do.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "У тебя болит живот?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Does your stomach hurt?' In Russian, 'you' leads into 'belly' in a very natural everyday phrasing. And Senya jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Да, мне очень плохо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, I feel very bad.' Here 'to me' sets up the idea, while 'badly' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я же тебе говорил.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I told you so.' Notice the word order: 'I' comes first, and 'said' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не надо было есть рыбу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You should not have eaten the fish.' The key word here means 'it is necessary', which Fedya combines with 'was'. Senya answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я думал, она нормальная.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I thought it was normal.' Senya starts with 'I' and pairs it with 'thought' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Знаешь, что надо делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you know what to do?' Fedya puts 'know' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'what'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Надо выпить перец и воду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You need to drink pepper and water.' Here 'it is necessary' sets up the idea, while 'water' comes at the end for emphasis. Then Senya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ой, я больше не могу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh, I can not take it anymore.' The first content word means 'oh', and 'can' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сеня, что с тобой?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Senya, what is wrong with you?' Fedya puts 'Senya' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'what'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сеня, открой глаза! Сеня!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Senya, open your eyes! Senya!' Listen for the word meaning 'Senya' right alongside 'to open' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Понятно, давай дальше.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Got it, let's move on.' The first content word means 'clear', and 'next' rounds out the thought. Now let us listen to the conversation once again.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
